One important naming issue

The two canonical documents currently use slightly different RAM rule prefixes.

The Sentinel specification uses:

ATL-RAM-001

The Atlas RAM model’s catalog uses:

ATLAS-RAM-001

We should not allow both forms into executable code.

Because the dedicated Sentinel Rule Specification explicitly defines ATL-RAM-*, I recommend treating that as the executable Sentinel identifier convention:

ATL-RAM-001
ATL-RAM-002
...
ATL-RAM-014

The Atlas RAM document should later be aligned so documentation, tests, logs, and Forge all use the same IDs. This is a documentation normalization issue, not an architectural defect.

